# Input field borders

Every standalone text input, select, textarea, and search field must show a visible **0.25px** border. Fields sit on `bg-white` or `bg-slate-50`, so a white, translucent, or `slate-200` border looks like no border.

## Required

```tsx
<Input className="border-[0.25px] border-slate-300" />
<SelectTrigger className="border-[0.25px] border-slate-300" />
<Textarea className="border-[0.25px] border-slate-300" />
<SearchField /> // wrapper already includes border-[0.25px] border-slate-300
```

- Width: `border-[0.25px]` (not Tailwind `border`, which is 1px)
- Resting color: `border-slate-300` (`#cbd5e1`) — stronger than card `slate-200` so fields read as inputs
- Hover: `hover:border-blue-300`
- Focus: `focus-visible:border-[#078FAB]`
- Shared class `.glass-form-control` already sets `0.25px solid #cbd5e1`; do not override it to 1px, white, transparent, or `slate-200`
- Search fields match select height: `h-10` (dropdowns are the source of truth)

## Forbidden on a standalone field

```tsx
<Input className="border-none" />
<Input className="border-0" />
<Input className="border" /> // 1px — too thick
<Input className="border-white/50" />
<Input className="border-slate-200" />
```

`border-0` is allowed only on an inner control whose parent already has the visible border (the inner `Input` inside `SearchField`).

`.shad-input` is `border-none` on purpose when it lives inside `.shad-form-item`, which already has `border-[0.25px] border-light-300`. Do not use `.shad-input` as a standalone field.
